       PROCESS APOST
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. COBOLINFO.
       AUTHOR.     BOB.
       DATE-WRITTEN. 2025.
      *==============================================================
      * COBOLINFO - ILE COBOL Reference: interactive 5250 display
      *
      * Displays scrollable COBOL reference topics retrieved from the
      * COBINFOSRV service program.  Display logic is fully separated
      * from content: content is obtained by calling an exported
      * procedure in COBINFOSRV.
      *
      * Controls:
      *   F3       - Exit
      *   PgDn     - Scroll down one page
      *   PgUp     - Scroll up one page
      *
      * Compile:
      *   CRTBNDCBL PGM(lib/COBOLINFO)
      *             SRCSTMF('path/cobolinfo.cblle')
      *             BNDDIR(lib/COBINFOBD)
      *             DBGVIEW(*SOURCE) OPTION(*APOST)
      *             TGTCCSID(*JOB)  AUT(*EXCLUDE)
      *==============================================================

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER. IBM-I.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER. IBM-I.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.
           LINKAGE TYPE IS PROCEDURE FOR 'COBINFOSRV'.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT COBSCRF
               ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-COBINFODSP
               ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
               FILE STATUS IS WS-SCR-STATUS.

       DATA DIVISION.
       FILE SECTION.
       FD  COBSCRF.
       01  COBSCR-REC.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF COBINFODSP.

       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01  WS-SCR-STATUS          PIC XX.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Response indicator area - 3 bytes, matching DDS listing:
      *   *IN03 = byte 1  (CA03  - F3 Exit)
      *   *IN25 = byte 2  (PAGEDOWN - scroll down)
      *   *IN26 = byte 3  (PAGEUP   - scroll up)
      * Each byte is '1' (on) or '0' (off).
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-IND-AREA.
           05  WS-IND-F3          PIC X.
           05  WS-IND-PGDN        PIC X.
           05  WS-IND-PGUP        PIC X.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Scrolling state
      * WS-NEW-TOP is SIGNED so subtraction below zero works correctly
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       77  WS-TOP-LINE            PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-TOTAL-LINES         PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       77  WS-PAGE-SIZE           PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 18.
       77  WS-TOTAL-PAGES         PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       77  WS-CUR-PAGE            PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 0.
       77  WS-IDX                 PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-LINE-IDX            PIC 9(3)  COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-NEW-TOP             PIC S9(3) COMP-4 VALUE 1.
       77  WS-PAGE-NUM-EDIT       PIC ZZ9.
       77  WS-TOTAL-EDIT          PIC ZZ9.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Screen output work fields
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-SCR-WORK.
           05  WS-HDRTOPIC        PIC X(30).
           05  WS-PAGENBR         PIC X(3).
           05  WS-TOTPAGES        PIC X(3).
           05  WS-MSGFLD          PIC X(25).
           05  WS-LINE            PIC X(77)
               OCCURS 18 TIMES.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Topic group item - interface contract with COBINFOSRV.
      * Identical layout to LINKAGE SECTION in cobinfosrv.cblle.
      * PICCLAUS-DATA fills WS-TOPIC-COUNT and WS-ENTRY(1..60).
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       01  WS-TOPIC.
           05  WS-TOPIC-COUNT     PIC 9(3)  COMP-4.
           05  WS-ENTRY           PIC X(77)
               OCCURS 60 TIMES.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN-SECTION SECTION.
       MAIN-PARA.
           MOVE 'COBOL PICTURE Clauses' TO WS-HDRTOPIC
           CALL 'COBINFOSRV' USING BY REFERENCE WS-TOPIC
           MOVE WS-TOPIC-COUNT TO WS-TOTAL-LINES
           PERFORM CALC-PAGES
           PERFORM OPEN-SCREEN
           PERFORM SCROLL-LOOP UNTIL WS-IND-F3 = '1'
           PERFORM CLOSE-SCREEN
           GOBACK.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Open the workstation file
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       OPEN-SCREEN.
           OPEN I-O COBSCRF
           IF WS-SCR-STATUS NOT = '00'
               DISPLAY 'COBSCRF open failed: ' WS-SCR-STATUS
               GOBACK
           END-IF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Close the workstation file
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       CLOSE-SCREEN.
           CLOSE COBSCRF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Main interaction loop - repeat until F3 pressed
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       SCROLL-LOOP.
           PERFORM FILL-SCREEN
           PERFORM WRITE-SCREEN
           MOVE LOW-VALUE TO WS-IND-AREA
           PERFORM READ-SCREEN
           EVALUATE TRUE
               WHEN WS-IND-F3   = '1'
                   CONTINUE
               WHEN WS-IND-PGDN = '1'
                   PERFORM PAGE-DOWN
               WHEN WS-IND-PGUP = '1'
                   PERFORM PAGE-UP
               WHEN OTHER
                   CONTINUE
           END-EVALUATE.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Page down: advance one page, stop at last page.
      * If already at bottom, show message and leave position unchanged.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       PAGE-DOWN.
           COMPUTE WS-NEW-TOP = WS-TOP-LINE + WS-PAGE-SIZE
           IF WS-NEW-TOP <= WS-TOTAL-LINES
               MOVE SPACES         TO WS-MSGFLD
               MOVE WS-NEW-TOP     TO WS-TOP-LINE
           ELSE
               MOVE '*** Already at bottom ***' TO WS-MSGFLD
           END-IF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Page up: retreat one page.
      * If already at top, show message and leave position unchanged.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       PAGE-UP.
           IF WS-TOP-LINE = 1
               MOVE '*** Already at top ***' TO WS-MSGFLD
           ELSE
               MOVE SPACES TO WS-MSGFLD
               COMPUTE WS-NEW-TOP = WS-TOP-LINE - WS-PAGE-SIZE
               IF WS-NEW-TOP >= 1
                   MOVE WS-NEW-TOP TO WS-TOP-LINE
               ELSE
                   MOVE 1 TO WS-TOP-LINE
               END-IF
           END-IF.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Calculate total pages from total lines and page size
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       CALC-PAGES.
           COMPUTE WS-TOTAL-PAGES =
               (WS-TOTAL-LINES + WS-PAGE-SIZE - 1) / WS-PAGE-SIZE.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Fill the 18 screen lines from the table at WS-TOP-LINE.
      * Also updates the page number fields and topic header.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       FILL-SCREEN.
           COMPUTE WS-CUR-PAGE =
               (WS-TOP-LINE + WS-PAGE-SIZE - 1) / WS-PAGE-SIZE

           MOVE WS-CUR-PAGE    TO WS-PAGE-NUM-EDIT
           MOVE WS-TOTAL-PAGES TO WS-TOTAL-EDIT
           MOVE WS-PAGE-NUM-EDIT TO WS-PAGENBR
           MOVE WS-TOTAL-EDIT    TO WS-TOTPAGES

           PERFORM VARYING WS-LINE-IDX FROM 1 BY 1
                   UNTIL WS-LINE-IDX > WS-PAGE-SIZE
               COMPUTE WS-IDX = WS-TOP-LINE + WS-LINE-IDX - 1
               IF WS-IDX <= WS-TOTAL-LINES
                   MOVE WS-ENTRY(WS-IDX) TO WS-LINE(WS-LINE-IDX)
               ELSE
                   MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE(WS-LINE-IDX)
               END-IF
           END-PERFORM.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Write the screen record to the display file.
      * WS-HDRTOPIC was set in MAIN-PARA and remains constant for
      * this topic; future topics will change it before calling here.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       WRITE-SCREEN.
           MOVE WS-HDRTOPIC  TO HDRTOPIC OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-PAGENBR   TO PAGENBR  OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-TOTPAGES  TO TOTPAGES OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-MSGFLD    TO MSGFLD   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(1)   TO LINE01   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(2)   TO LINE02   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(3)   TO LINE03   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(4)   TO LINE04   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(5)   TO LINE05   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(6)   TO LINE06   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(7)   TO LINE07   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(8)   TO LINE08   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(9)   TO LINE09   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(10)  TO LINE10   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(11)  TO LINE11   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(12)  TO LINE12   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(13)  TO LINE13   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(14)  TO LINE14   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(15)  TO LINE15   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(16)  TO LINE16   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(17)  TO LINE17   OF COBSCR-REC
           MOVE WS-LINE(18)  TO LINE18   OF COBSCR-REC
           WRITE COBSCR-REC FORMAT IS 'COBSCR'.

      *--------------------------------------------------------------
      * Read the screen; INDICATORS ARE receives the response
      * indicator bytes back from the display file.
      *--------------------------------------------------------------
       READ-SCREEN.
           READ COBSCRF FORMAT IS 'COBSCR'
               INDICATORS ARE WS-IND-AREA
               AT END
                   MOVE '1' TO WS-IND-F3
           END-READ.

       END PROGRAM COBOLINFO.
